# --- Secret-prevention classes (RUN PUBLIC-SECURITY-HARDENING R5/Task 4) ---
# Dotenv files. If a committed example is ever wanted, add `!.env.example`.
.env
.env.*
# Key / certificate / credential material.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
credentials.json
credentials.yaml
credentials.yml
*.credentials
# Local database sidecars. No fixture DB is tracked today
# (`git ls-files '*.db' '*.sqlite*'` is empty); if one is ever committed,
# add an anchored `!path/to/fixture.db` negation here — never un-ignore
# the class globally.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Build-run process records. Plans, dev notes, QA reports and findings --
# archaeology of HOW a run was built. Durable output lives elsewhere: data
# contracts and decisions in docs/architecture/, the dashboard contract in
# docs/frontend/, open work in docs/roadmap.md. These records serve no
# reader outside this checkout and were the largest low-value surface the
# public tree carried.
#
# `dir/*`, never `dir/` -- git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so a negation under a directory-form exclude is silently inert.
#
# Exception: the M2-12 stub is the record that R14/R15 scope was WITHDRAWN,
# not lost, and carries the LD-8/TD-7 retention obligation. It is pinned by
# test_refresh_stub_exists_and_carries_retention_obligation -- the document
# is the control, so untracking it would turn that gate green by deletion.
docs/build/*
!docs/build/RUN-M2-12-inst-refresh-stub.md
# Operator runbooks. Deploy, attestation, GitHub security, data maintenance,
# the Kadoa backfill audit and the gate-tier description describe this
# deployment's live infrastructure in operational detail. They contain no
# secrets, but they are free reconnaissance on a public repository, so they
# are maintained outside the published tree. Earlier revisions remain in Git
# history.
#
# `dir/*`, never `dir/` -- git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so a negation under a directory-form exclude is silently inert.
#
# Exceptions: the R18 gate asserts that these two exist and that their
# executable snippets are gated (test_publish.py::test_runbook_exists_with_
# gated_executable_snippets). The document is the control, so untracking it
# would retire the gate rather than hide it.
docs/operations/*
!docs/operations/rollback.md
!docs/operations/disaster-recovery.md
# Tool-local state and review outputs.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.codex-review/
planned-files.json
